  "query_preview": "..A shortwave trough located over Arizona today will \nhead to the east of our area tonight. Look for southwest winds at\n15-25 mph gusting to 30-45 mph to continue into the early evening\nbefore diminishing overnight(the higher values in the ranges will\nmainly be observed from the Mogollon Rim northward). As a result,\na Wind Advisory and Red Flag Warning will remain in effect \ninto the early evening hours. For the remainder of the night, \npressure gradients will remain strong enough for gusty west to \nsouthwest winds from the Mogollon Rim northward where we're look \nat wind speeds of 10-20 mph gusting to around 25 mph.\n\nFor Thursday and Friday...The current trough will head eastward.\nAs a result, winds will shift to more southwest to west direction\nbecoming lighter at 10-20 mph gusting to around 25 mph most \nareas. Look for mainly sunny skies on Thursday but some \nadditional cloudiness will move in on Friday with a weak passing \ndisturbance. Little change in high and low temperatures.\n\nFrom Saturday onward...Models continue to show a series of weak \nshortwave troughs moving across the southwest United States. Near\nto below seasonal average temperatures appear on track as a cooler\nair mass is expected to move in. The best chances for showers \nappears to be Saturday and Sunday but with such weak features \nthis is apt to change. In any case, breezy daytime winds each day.",
